The eigenvectors $bold(u_1), ..., bold(u_n)$ can be chosen orthonormal, $bold(u_i^dagger) bold(u_j) = delta_(i j)$. Equivalently the matrix $matbold(P)$ of eigenvectors can be chosen unitary, $matbold(P)^dagger = matbold(P)^(-1)$, so

$ matbold(P^dagger) matbold(A) matbold(P) = matbold(D). $

For a real symmetric matrix the eigenvectors can be taken in $RR^n$ with $bold(u_i^tp) bold(u_j) = delta_(i j)$, equivalently $matbold(P)$ orthogonal with $matbold(P)^tp = matbold(P)^(-1)$ and $matbold(P^tp) matbold(A) matbold(P) = matbold(D)$.
